  "worked_solution": "The minor of ${c}_{12}=2$ (first row, second column) is the determinant of the remaining entries when the column and row containing $2$ are removed: \n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}\u2217 & 2 & \u2217 \\\\ 0 & \u2217 & 4 \\\\ 7 & \u2217 & 6\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSo, the minor of ${c}_{12}=2$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{12} & =\\text{det}[\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 \\\\ 7 & 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 \\\\ 7 & 6\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =0\\cdot 6-4\\cdot 7 \\\\  & =0-28 \\\\  & =-28.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
